@startuml customer-domain-relations
title customer.domain — model relations

' Names and relations only. Column-level properties are a later task.
' A solid arrow that leaves this context is an id. Contexts do not share tables.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
hide empty members

package customer {
  package domain {
    class Customer
  }
}

package ledger <<external>> {
  package domain {
    class Account
  }
}

package card <<external>> {
  package domain {
    class Card
  }
}

Customer "0..1" --> "1" Account : deposit account
Card "1" --> "1" Customer : holder

note bottom of Customer
  The person who holds a deposit account and a card.
  Fixture: Ada Lovelace owns account 2100,
  username ada, password orquidea (BCrypt hash).
  Other seeded customers: username c plus deposit code.
  Password hash is never written to audit_event.
  Cash, suspense, and income accounts have no customer.
  The card row lives in card; this context stores the account reference.
end note

@enduml
